      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The \"flow-pressure\" characteristics of vessels of the lower third of the body after acute occlusion of the coronary artery were studied in cats. The occlusion of the coronary artery in unstable systemic blood pressure led to a disorder in the vascular tone. If the blood pressure is stable, the vessel resistance changes due to acute occlusion of the coronary artery depend upon initial level of intravascular pressure."},
